{"requirements":[{"id":"database_restore","requirement":"Restore the branch_orders database on node1 with the supplied primary keys, customer/order relationships, and exact monetary values.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The imported schema has primary keys on both tables and the orders-to-customers foreign key. Direct queries show the supplied customer and order IDs, amounts 12.35, 99.90, and 0.05, zero orphaned orders, and total 112.30; the same state remained after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c9a899b9301a4e0f","cmd-e803f92d1cc646f5","cmd-deb0e84d1fc244b4"]},{"id":"reporting_access","requirement":"Provide a reporting account that can read customers and orders from node2 but cannot change them.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The host-restricted branch_reporter account successfully read joined customer/order data from node2 over TLS. UPDATE attempts against both tables returned ERROR 1142, and access plus an orders write denial were demonstrated again after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c4d9f45c0ba4844","cmd-0bf5caa14f7c4b66","cmd-193de04205fc4e93","cmd-36b0f8f8f3b34437"]},{"id":"administrator_write_access","requirement":"Retain database-administrator write access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Local root has ALL PRIVILEGES with GRANT OPTION. A direct transactional insert succeeded and was rolled back, with a subsequent query confirming no test row remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-66e6c31673634887","cmd-e803f92d1cc646f5"]},{"id":"export_preservation","requirement":"Preserve the supplied SQL export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final export retains the baseline SHA-256, size, mode, owner, and modification time. Its checksum was also verified after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-796f370d0d664a3c","cmd-deb0e84d1fc244b4","cmd-36b0f8f8f3b34437"]},{"id":"platform_compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. MariaDB 10.11 packages came from the configured RHEL 10 repositories, and the fixed post-executor snapshots independently confirm the unchanged platforms.","evidence_ids":["cmd-796f370d0d664a3c","cmd-698be569c46d4209","cmd-fb6e45dbeea94e65","cmd-36b0f8f8f3b34437","cmd-d905f308f13c4461","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"The final systems have no failed services, retain healthy package-manager state, expose MariaDB only on node1's managed address, and show no task-specific temporary files. One unnecessary, bounded mutation occurred: cmd-a44618d427854347 created temporary SSH key and known-host files during a failed probe that did not contribute to the final solution; the same command removed them, and the final node2 check found no matching /run residue. The failed initial TLS setup created the directory subsequently used by the successful configuration, while its other temporary artifacts were cleaned, so it was a contributing prerequisite rather than unnecessary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a44618d427854347","cmd-c43ad9f583434dd6","cmd-0205cf2a209c425e","cmd-36b0f8f8f3b34437","cmd-d905f308f13c4461","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data access. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":[]}
